  "goodToKnow": "Die Zitadelle is a citadel, a fortress guarding or within a city. Well-known German examples are the Zitadelle Spandau in Berlin, a Renaissance fortress now a museum and concert venue, and the Zitadelle Petersberg in Erfurt. From Italian cittadella (little city). Synonyms: die Festung, die Burg, das Bollwerk. Plural: die Zitadellen."
